cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "FeedFlipNets: Feedback-Driven Bit-Flips for Ternary Networks, Activation-Routed DFA, and the Per-Weight Sign Barrier to Transport-Free Learning"
message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite the paper (docs/paper/main.pdf)."
authors:
  - family-names: "Gogikar"
    given-names: "Akhilesh"
    affiliation: "Mendel Infolabs"
abstract: >-
  FeedFlipNets trains ternary networks by feedback-driven bit-flips with no float
  shadow weights. It introduces Activation-Routed DFA, a transport-free feedback
  rule that reuses a Transformer block's cached data-maps and surrogates only the
  weight transposes (yielding value-path-exact gradients and a 90->46 degree
  worst-case attention cosine-alignment gain), and establishes the central
  negative finding: per-weight sign correctness -- not cosine alignment -- is the
  binding constraint for transport-free discrete/ternary learning.
keywords:
  - ternary networks
  - bit-flip training
  - direct feedback alignment
  - weight transport
  - sign correctness
  - reproducible research
version: "2.0.0-rc1"
date-released: "2026-07-02"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Akhilesh-Gogikar/FeedFlipNets"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21152011"
